<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo in $20 mln Uzbekistan bank JV.</title>
<headline>Daewoo in $20 mln Uzbekistan bank JV.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daewoo Securities, a unit of the Daewoo Group, said on Tuesday it would take a 55 percent stake in an Uzbekistan bank joint venture.</p>
<p>Other partners in the UzDaewoo Bank, to be capitalised at $20 million, are the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development, which will hold a 25 percent stake, and KorAm Bank, with 10 percent.</p>
<p>Uzbekistan banks NBU and Turan Bank will each hold five percent of the joint venture.</p>
<p>The bank is expected to begin business on January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
